{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1389077-players-keep-forgetting-to-resolve-their-conditions","id":1389077,"title":"Players keep forgetting to resolve their conditions ...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-16T14:55:47-07:00","id":1389077,"title":"Players keep forgetting to resolve their conditions ...","content":"Hello everyone,<br /> <br /> my players have a tendency to forget their conditions. Like one became &quot;shaken&quot; at a ritualistic crime scene. But since &quot;shaken&quot; doesn't have any negative effects, there is no constant reminder that their character has the condition during play. (And yes my players do have a copy of that condition card.) \ud83d\ude06<br /> Furthermore, we rarely roll dice unless it's really important and they don't like to fail at those moments. But that's how you would resolve that condition. In the game world, weeks have already passed and it becomes kind of ridiculous to still keep it.<br /> <br /> 1) How do you handle those things?<br /> 2) Do you use those conditions somehow as a storytelling device to remind your players? If so, how?<br /> (Up until now, I thought of it as a roleplaying hint for the players. But that doesn't always seem to work.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Waiting for new Chronicles of Darkness Dice! \ud83e\udd17 \ud83c\udfb2","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1825-elythia","name":"Elythia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1825_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T15:03:23-07:00","id":1389079,"title":"","content":"Printing them out or writing them on an index card and handing them to the player has helped us.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T15:15:48-07:00","id":1389086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1389077-players-keep-forgetting-to-resolve-their-conditions?p=1389079#post1389079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Printing them out or writing them on an index card and handing them to the player has helped us.</div> </div> </div> </div>As mentioned before, I already did that. \ud83d\ude06","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Waiting for new Chronicles of Darkness Dice! \ud83e\udd17 \ud83c\udfb2","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1825-elythia","name":"Elythia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1825_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T16:58:33-07:00","id":1389121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elythia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1389077-players-keep-forgetting-to-resolve-their-conditions?p=1389086#post1389086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As mentioned before, I already did that. \ud83d\ude06</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry, I missed that.<br /> <br /> If they're going so far as to ignore a physical representation of the effect and its depiction of how to gain Experience through it, it seems like there would be nothing you could really do. There's an actual manifested reminder, and something to gain from it. At that point it's less a matter of forgetting as much as ignoring. One option would be to just keep stacking up penalties until they realized 'Why do I have so many penalties?' and maybe tried to do something to resolve them, but not every Condition should involve penalties like that.<br /> <br /> So I suppose I would suggest just removing said Conditions from the table after an amount of time you consider appropriate. They lose the ability to resolve it.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, you could alter the Conditions given to make them more receptive to your party, though that would rely more on what your party finds memorable, but it would let you slip in some more noticeable things like bonuses or penalties.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-16-2020, 08:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T22:47:20-07:00","id":1389202,"title":"","content":"Thank you for your suggestions! I will consider them. \ud83d\ude42<br /> <br /> Yesterday I watched an episode of \u201eHunter: The Vigil\u201c on the Onyx Path YouTube channel. When on of the players got the \u201eSpooked Condition\u201c the storyteller says that it doesn\u2019t have a negative effect, but it is one of those conditions that are fuel for the storyteller. Sadly the episode ends before anything like that happens. I think using it as a storytelling device would really be a great option. But how?<br /> This is also where my second question is coming from! \ud83e\udd14<br /> <br /> YouTube episode (with timestamp): <a href=\"https://youtu.be/LJs8Q6KVu1o?t=83m32s\" target=\"_blank\">https://youtu.be/LJs8Q6KVu1o?t=83m32s</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Waiting for new Chronicles of Darkness Dice! \ud83e\udd17 \ud83c\udfb2","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1825-elythia","name":"Elythia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1825_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T20:23:01-07:00","id":1390166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1389077-players-keep-forgetting-to-resolve-their-conditions?p=1389079#post1389079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Printing them out or writing them on an index card and handing them to the player has helped us.</div> </div> </div> </div>Similar to what has already been said cards, or props it may sound funny but if you hand the player a small stuffed ghost there is bound to be some laughs and hard to ignore the damn stuffed ghost in the way. <br /> <br /> Coming up with a few creative, inexpensive props could be fun, include the players in the prop search. <br /> <br /> Also as mentioned you snooze you loose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Storypath &amp; Storypath to Run CoD, VtR, WtF, MtA</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","name":"Graylion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"368"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-20T14:55:28-07:00","id":1390388,"title":"","content":"The problem isn't conditions. The problem is you rarely roll dice, which is not a problem in and of itself but as a consequence makes experience and thus conditions hold less weight - when rolls rarely happen and are usually weighted so that you'll most likely succeed then experience loses its value and thus so do Conditions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/11.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16101-eternal-darkness","name":"Eternal Darkness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-21T06:13:50-07:00","id":1390541,"title":"","content":"If you've got the type of players that respond to mechanical issues, I'd just suggest creating situational modifiers based on them. E.g. say to your player &quot;Because you're currently shaken, you've got a -1 to perception while scoping out this graveyard&quot;.<br /> <br /> Doesn't have to be big or gamechanging, just a mechanical stick to go with the mechanical carrot of getting EXP. Having played a few 2E games so far, it can be difficult to consistently interact with conditions while still keeping track of the rest of the game mechanics during play. My tables tend to forget them all the time too (enough so that one game the ST decided to just award so many beats each session as well just to keep our EXP ticking).<br /> <br /> It would probably be an idea to try and prompt rolls too - if they're failing a lot (or get really cranky about it) get them to RP their way into bonuses rather than just resolving them without rolling dice. At least that'd give more chances to resolve conditions like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-21T13:29:30-07:00","id":1390613,"title":"","content":"Thanks for all of your advices. \ud83d\ude42<br /> I really like the idea with the small debuffs! \ud83d\ude0a <br /> I think I will create a short non exclusive list of ideas, where I could potentially use them. <br /> <br /> Maybe I should also try to integrate them somehow into the text of my scenes for the next session, if possible.<br /> <br /> \u2014\u2014\u2014<br /> <br /> Just for clarification (off-topic): <br /> - It\u2019s not like we don\u2019t roll dice, but maybe a little bit below average compared to other groups, since we focus on the story. <br /> (Compared to those YouTube videos, with not even five minutes between dice rolls, we rarely roll.)<br /> - They got the condition on a crime scene, but since they are playing homicide detectives, so they usually don\u2019t fail any investigation rolls. <br /> - I don\u2019t want to reward people for roleplaying, because it\u2019s subjective. Furthermore they are more analytical players that still need help to contribute something to the scene to flash out their character or for the sake of the atmosphere. They are still very \u201creactive\u201d and not \u201cproactive\u201d in that matter. Thankfully we have Aspirations now. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Waiting for new Chronicles of Darkness Dice! \ud83e\udd17 \ud83c\udfb2","edited":{"userid":1825,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1825-elythia","user":"Elythia","date":". 05-21-2020, 05:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1825-elythia","name":"Elythia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1825_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-21T17:41:06-07:00","id":1390665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elythia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1389077-players-keep-forgetting-to-resolve-their-conditions?p=1389202#post1389202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you for your suggestions! I will consider them. \ud83d\ude42<br /> <br /> Yesterday I watched an episode of \u201eHunter: The Vigil\u201c on the Onyx Path YouTube channel. When on of the players got the \u201eSpooked Condition\u201c the storyteller says that it doesn\u2019t have a negative effect, but it is one of those conditions that are fuel for the storyteller. Sadly the episode ends before anything like that happens. I think using it as a storytelling device would really be a great option. But how?<br /> This is also where my second question is coming from! \ud83e\udd14<br /> <br /> YouTube episode (with timestamp): <a href=\"https://youtu.be/LJs8Q6KVu1o?t=83m32s\" target=\"_blank\">https://youtu.be/LJs8Q6KVu1o?t=83m32s</a></div> </div> </div> </div>I did not know Onyx Path had a YouTube channel, if there\u2019s a lot of CofD on it I will be binging.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-21T19:35:39-07:00","id":1390684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elythia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1389077-players-keep-forgetting-to-resolve-their-conditions?p=1390613#post1390613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- I don\u2019t want to reward people for roleplaying, because it\u2019s subjective. Furthermore they are more analytical players that still need help to contribute something to the scene to flash out their character or for the sake of the atmosphere. They are still very \u201creactive\u201d and not \u201cproactive\u201d in that matter. Thankfully we have Aspirations now. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I award my players 0-2 Beats per session by casual roleplaying their Anchors - Virtue &amp; Vice, Blood &amp; Bone, Life &amp; Legend, etc. Players point what their PCs done in accordance to traits in session - and when in question, I ask rest of the team if they are convinced. It also makes Anchors more relevant on day-to-day basis, as generating Willpowers scenes are rare. It works rather good for us and seems fair. 8-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 05-21-2020, 10:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-27T23:34:39-07:00","id":1392133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1389077-players-keep-forgetting-to-resolve-their-conditions?p=1390684#post1390684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I award my players 0-2 Beats per session by casual roleplaying their Anchors - Virtue &amp; Vice, Blood &amp; Bone, Life &amp; Legend, etc. Players point what their PCs done in accordance to traits in session - and when in question, I ask rest of the team if they are convinced. It also makes Anchors more relevant on day-to-day basis, as generating Willpowers scenes are rare. It works rather good for us and seems fair. 8-)</div> </div> </div> </div>I will consider that! \ud83d\ude42","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Waiting for new Chronicles of Darkness Dice! \ud83e\udd17 \ud83c\udfb2","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1825-elythia","name":"Elythia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1825_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}